253 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (INCENTIVISING PROGRESS IN ESG AREAS: Developing countries face a dual burden: the need to service existing debt while also financing the costly transition to a low-carbon economy. Incentives are needed to encourage domestic policies that support a wide range of ESG objectives, such as decarbonizing the power sector, improving social equity, and enhancing governance standards, while progressing toward a developed economy.)
/E (INCENTIVISING PROGRESS IN ESG AREAS: Developing countries face a dual burden: the need to service existing debt while also financing the costly transition to a low-carbon economy. Incentives are needed to encourage domestic policies that support a wide range of ESG objectives, such as decarbonizing the power sector, improving social equity, and enhancing governance standards, while progressing toward a developed economy.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [2]
