/T (Key Issues to be Addressed)
/E (Key Issues to be Addressed)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
355 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (INCENTIVES FOR CLIMATE ACTION: Achieving global net-zero emissions necessitates coordinated national policy actions and increased investments in clean energy. Developing countries often grapple with the challenge of prioritizing development goals, which can  sideline critical climate initiatives.)
/E (INCENTIVES FOR CLIMATE ACTION: Achieving global net-zero emissions necessitates coordinated national policy actions and increased investments in clean energy. Developing countries often grapple with the challenge of prioritizing development goals, which can  sideline critical climate initiatives.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
356 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (FINANCIAL SCALE: Ideally, any national government or municipality aiming for a swift transition to net zero \(by 2050 or sooner\) but struggling to attract significant private investment or access low-cost financing, should receive financial support from the World Bank or associated institutions. However, the availability of such funding remains limited.)
/E (FINANCIAL SCALE: Ideally, any national government or municipality aiming for a swift transition to net zero \(by 2050 or sooner\) but struggling to attract significant private investment or access low-cost financing, should receive financial support from the World Bank or associated institutions. However, the availability of such funding remains limited.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
